  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'slow travel' is gaining popularity among tourists who want to experience a destination in a more authentic way. Slow travel encourages visitors to linger in one place for longer periods, immersing themselves in the local culture and community. This approach allows travelers to appreciate the nuances of a region's history, architecture, and cuisine, rather than rushing from one tourist attraction to another.\n\nIn contrast, mass tourism can have negative consequences on local environments and communities. Overcrowding, pollution, and strain on resources are just a few of the issues that arise when large numbers of visitors descend upon a popular destination. By adopting slow travel practices, tourists can help reduce their impact on the places they visit.\n\nAs more people begin to adopt this approach, there is a growing need for sustainable tourism infrastructure. This includes eco-friendly accommodations, public transportation systems, and community-led initiatives that promote cultural exchange and understanding. By supporting these efforts, travelers can contribute to the preservation of destinations for future generations.\n\nIn addition to its environmental benefits, slow travel also offers a more enriching experience for visitors. By engaging with local people and immersing themselves in the culture, tourists can gain a deeper appreciation for the complexities and challenges faced by communities around the world. This, in turn, fosters empathy, understanding, and a sense of global citizenship.\n\nAs we move forward in an increasingly interconnected world, slow travel offers a compelling alternative to mass tourism. By embracing this approach, travelers can not only reduce their environmental footprint but also enrich their own lives through meaningful cultural exchange.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the article about?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The benefits of mass tourism\", \"The negative consequences of over-tourism\", \"The concept of slow travel and its advantages\", \"The importance of cultural exchange in global citizenship\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the article, what is one of the negative effects of mass tourism on local environments?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Overcrowding and strain on resources\", \"Pollution and destruction of natural habitats\", \"Economic growth and job creation\", \"Increased demand for sustainable infrastructure\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"The author suggests that slow travel can help reduce the impact of tourism on local communities. What is one way in which this can be achieved?\",\n      \"options\": [\"By supporting community-led initiatives and eco-friendly accommodations\", \"By promoting cultural exchange and understanding through public events\", \"By reducing the number of tourists visiting a destination\", \"By increasing the length of stay for individual tourists\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"The article states that slow travel offers a more enriching experience for visitors. What is one way in which this can be achieved?\",\n      \"options\": [\"By engaging with local people and immersing themselves in the culture\", \"By visiting popular tourist attractions and taking guided tours\", \"By staying in luxury hotels and resorts\", \"By using public transportation systems to get around\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"The author's attitude towards mass tourism is best described as:\",\n      \"options\": [\"Supportive and encouraging\", \"Critical and dismissive\", \"Neutral and informative\", \"Ambivalent and uncertain\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option2\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
